   "id": "d01e03f443cd6f84",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Converting cyclical time variable to linear difference from midday"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "58f2d36b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The hours are are in String datatype and in format XX.00-XX.59.\n",
    "\n",
    "We take the first two characters of each string in column 'kello' and convert that to float. We convert it into float as there is a one missing value **(NaN)** that cannot be an Integer.\n",
    "\n",
    "After dropping the missing row, conversion to whole numbers is done with **.astype(int)**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 149,
   "id": "e9fa7bd2",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-10-08T11:54:02.713615Z",
     "start_time": "2026-10-08T11:54:02.706704700Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_accidents['tunti'] = df_accidents['kello'].str[:2].astype(float)\n",
    "\n",
    "# drop the row(s) with missing time, then make it an integer\n",
    "df_accidents = df_accidents.dropna(subset=['tunti'])\n",
    "df_accidents['tunti'] = df_accidents['tunti'].astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Subtracts each accident's hour from 12 and takes the absolute value\n",
    "df_accidents['tunti'] = (12 - df_accidents['tunti']).abs()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop the column 'kello'.\n",
    "df_accidents = df_accidents.drop(columns=['kello'])"
   ]
  },
  {
